From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Gino D." <25200363+zinosaure@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 05:11:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gameflex 0092: no submission that feeds nothing (P4.1)

0088 counted, per frame in Clair Obscur, 5 empty buffers submitted at suspend points and 2 WaitFlipDone
flushes with no flip pending (Astro Bot: 1); each vkQueueSubmit costs ~200 us of the command thread.

- A suspend point whose buffer is empty, with no operation waiting for it, releases the game once the work
  already submitted is done (DeferPriorityOperationOnSubmitted, on the last submitted tick); the buffer stays
  open for the next frame. The occlusion counters are still published.
- WaitFlipDone flushes only when a flip of the buffer is pending: the flip queue calls the flush, outside its
  lock, when it has to wait. A flip queued after its check is not waited for, as when the check came first.
  HasPendingFlip and FlipQueue::HasRequest go.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
